---
// Beat 3 — How it works (the loop).
// Four illustrated steps + rituals line, verbatim from docs/copy-deck.md.
// Icons: pack, waypoint (manifest), stamp (reports — trail-600, NOT the
// reserved --color-report token, which is exclusive to the Beat 2 demo's
// report line), compass (survey).
// Responsive: 4-up desktop, stacked mobile.

import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
---

<section id="how-it-works" data-beat="3-how-it-works">
  <div class="container-field">
    <h2 class="font-heading text-3xl font-semibold text-forest-600 mb-12">
      The loop.
    </h2>

    <!-- Four illustrated steps — responsive grid (4 cols desktop, 1 col mobile) -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-8 mb-8">
      <!-- Step 1: Pack it -->
      <div class="flex flex-col">
        <div class="mb-4 text-trail-500">
          <Icon name="pack" size={32} class="text-trail-500" />
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-heading text-xl font-semibold text-ink mb-3">
          Pack it
        </h3>
        <p class="text-base text-ink leading-relaxed">
          <code class="code-inline">
            /scout:add
          </code>
          {' '}a URL from anywhere. Scout reads it, drafts the entry, and files it
          with the conditions where it applies.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 2: The manifest -->
      <div class="flex flex-col">
        <div class="mb-4 text-trail-500">
          <Icon name="waypoint" size={32} class="text-trail-500" />
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-heading text-xl font-semibold text-ink mb-3">
          The manifest
        </h3>
        <p class="text-base text-ink leading-relaxed">
          <code class="code-inline">
            /scout:start
          </code>
          {' '}on a new project writes a compact packing list into your agent's
          context. Capped small on purpose: a pack you can't carry is a pack you
          don't bring.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 3: Reports -->
      <div class="flex flex-col">
        <div class="mb-4 text-trail-600">
          <Icon name="stamp" size={32} class="text-trail-600" />
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-heading text-xl font-semibold text-ink mb-3">
          Reports
        </h3>
        <p class="text-base text-ink leading-relaxed">
          While you build, matches that survive Scout's gate surface as one-line
          reports. Ignore them freely — Scout learns from that too.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 4: Survey -->
      <div class="flex flex-col">
        <div class="mb-4 text-forest-500">
          <Icon name="compass" size={32} class="text-forest-500" />
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-heading text-xl font-semibold text-ink mb-3">
          Survey
        </h3>
        <p class="text-base text-ink leading-relaxed">
          Before you ship,
          {' '}<code class="code-inline">
            /scout:survey
          </code>
          {' '}walks the whole project for anything you missed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Rituals line — quiet placement below the four steps -->
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-paper-300">
      Scout also carries your project rituals — changelog, decision log, how you
      build big features — so every project starts the same way.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
